{"name":"Temple Guard Blue","hex":"#339a8d","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"temple","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A house of worship, especially:\nA house of worship dedicated to a polytheistic faith.","A house of worship dedicated to a polytheistic faith."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To build a temple for; to appropriate a temple to; to temple a god"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/temple"},{"term":"guard","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A person who, or thing that, protects or watches over something.","A garda; a police officer."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To protect from danger; to secure against surprise, attack, or injury; to keep in safety; to defend.","To keep watch over, in order to prevent escape or restrain from acts of violence, or the like."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/guard"},{"term":"blue","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a blue hue.","Depressed, melancholic, sad."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The colour of the clear sky or the deep sea; the colour midway between green and violet in the visible spectrum and one of the primary additive colours.","Anything coloured blue, especially to distinguish it from similar objects differing only in colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blue"}],"entries":[{"title":"Legends of the Hidden Temple","blocks":[{"text":"Legends of the Hidden Temple is an American action-adventure television game show that was produced from 1993 to 1995 on Nickelodeon. Created by David G. Stanley, Scott A. Stone, and Stephen Brown, the program features a fictitious temple, \"filled with lost treasures protected by mysterious Mayan temple guards.\" Kirk Fogg is the show's host, while Dee Baker is both announcer and voice of a stone head named Olmec who \"knows the secrets behind each of the treasures in his temple.\" Six teams of two children compete to retrieve one of the historical artifacts in the temple by performing physical stunts and answering questions based on history, mythology, and geography. Contestants trying out had to compete in several physical tasks, including rope climbing and running, as well as a written test. The majority of the contestants were picked from the surrounding Orlando, Florida, area."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/f/f5/Legends_of_the_Hidden_Temple_logo.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Legends_of_the_Hidden_Temple"},{"title":"Temple","blocks":[{"text":"A temple is a place of worship, a building used for spiritual rituals and activities such as prayer and sacrifice. By convention, the specially built places of worship for some religions are commonly called \"temples\" in English, while those of other religions are not, even though they fulfill very similar functions."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ae/Philae_temple_at_night.jpg/330px-Philae_temple_at_night.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Temple"},{"title":"Blue","blocks":[{"text":"Blue is one of the three primary colours in the RGB (additive) colour model, as well as in the RYB colour model. It lies between violet and cyan on the spectrum of visible light. The term blue generally describes colours perceived by humans observing light with a dominant wavelength between approximately 450 and 495 nanometres. The clear daytime sky and the deep sea appear blue because of an optical effect known as Rayleigh scattering. An optical effect called the Tyndall effect explains blue eyes. Distant objects appear more blue because of another optical effect called aerial perspective."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg/330px-Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/7/77/LegendsTitlecard.jpg/330px-LegendsTitlecard.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/7/77/LegendsTitlecard.jpg/330px-LegendsTitlecard.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Title card of Legends of the Hidden Temple","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALegendsTitlecard.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/1/1d/Legends_of_the_Hidden_Temple_%28assembling_monkey%29.jpg/250px-Legends_of_the_Hidden_Temple_%28assembling_monkey%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/1/1d/Legends_of_the_Hidden_Temple_%28assembling_monkey%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/1/1d/Legends_of_the_Hidden_Temple_%28assembling_monkey%29.jpg/250px-Legends_of_the_Hidden_Temple_%28assembling_monkey%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A contestant assembles a three-piece statue in the Shrine of the Silver Monkey. When the statue is assembled correctly, the unlocked doors of the room open and the contestant can advance toward the artifact, indicated by the pink circle on the map at the bottom left.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALegends_of_the_Hidden_Temple_(assembling_monkey).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/44/Ankor_Wat_temple.jpg/500px-Ankor_Wat_temple.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/44/Ankor_Wat_temple.jpg/500px-Ankor_Wat_temple.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbn